-- THE OPERATOR'S WORKSHEET: a person's reading of Erdős #488's sentence (claimbox's second kind of proposer, commitment 5).
-- Write it from the sentence below and lean/READING.md alone; it is compared with the blind model reading
-- (erdos-488.reading) only after it is written. Never overwritten by a tool. When done, run:
--   python3 -m claimbox intake read corpus/intake/erdos-488/erdos-488.person.reading
--
-- The sentence (erdosproblems.com/488, corpus/intake/erdos-488/sentence.json):
--   Let $A$ be a finite set and \[B=\{ n \geq 1 : a\mid n\textrm{ for some }a\in A\}.\] Is it true that, for every
--   $m>n\geq \max(A)$, \[\frac{\lvert B\cap [1,m]\rvert }{m}< 2\frac{\lvert B\cap [1,n]\rvert}{n}?\]
--
-- The instances come in the order A, n, m: declare them with `given` in that order. Where the sentence leaves a
-- domain open and the answer could change, write each choice with `|`.
reading erdos-488-person
source  erdosproblems = corpus/intake/erdos-488/sentence.json
quote   from erdosproblems
proposed by person
-- given   A : …
-- given   n, m : …
-- let     B = …
-- assume  …
-- claim   …
